      "role": "user",
      "content": "The fire in the brazier is dying, and so is everything else. I can still hear them... the sound of the horses falling, the screaming when the line broke. It was my call. I sent them into that gorge thinking I was a strategist, but I was just a butcher. I look at my hands and I don't see a commander anymore. I just see the blood of men who trusted me. There's no honor left in this camp, only the stench of my own failure. I don't know how I'm supposed to face the dawn.",
